# ---- .NET build output ----
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# ---- Per-user editor/agent config ----
# .claude/settings.json is the PROJECT's config and is tracked. settings.local.json is the per-user
# overlay Claude Code writes as you approve things; it is full of one machine's absolute paths and means
# nothing to anyone else.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---- Live instance state — NEVER committed ----
# The counterpart to game-data/. Created by running the server, unique to this machine, and the entire
# backup target (the nightly sqlite3 .backup lives in Project1998-infra, scripts/p1998-backup.sh):
#   state/   project1998.db + its WAL sidecars, the legacy chars/*.json store, gm/tester_accounts.txt
#   logs/    server.log / login.log and their rotations. Regenerable; 80 MB of them here right now.
#   run/     restart_at / reload_now — deploy-to-server triggers, consumed and deleted on read.
#
# These are top-level SIBLINGS of game-data/ rather than living inside it, and that is what makes this
# section three lines. When state sat in the same directory as content, the content tree needed its own
# .gitignore listing every runtime filename, the deploy rsync needed the matching exclude list, and both
# had to be updated in lockstep every time something new started being written. A directory the content
# tree cannot see needs no rules at all.
state/
logs/
run/

*.log
server_live.err
server-err.log

# Ad-hoc capture/scratch dropped at the repo root by a probe or a bot run.
scratch_*.html
char_levels.csv

# ---- Third-party trees cloned next to the source, never vendored ----
# RTK-Server: unkmc/RTK-Server, ~190 MB. The 7.x reference server; the single most-cited source in this
#   codebase, and the origin of most of game-data/. Clone it yourself — see docs/research/README.md.
# cnc-ddraw: 8 MB of prebuilt DirectDraw shim binaries for running the 2001 client on Windows 11.
# client-5.33-redirect: written by the 5.33 client at runtime.
RTK-Server/
re/cnc-ddraw/
client-5.33-redirect/

# =================================================================================================
# re/ — the reverse-engineering workbench
#
# What IS tracked here: the ~155 Python extractors, probes and Frida scripts, plus the small CSV/JSON/MD
# files that are the FINDINGS. Forty-five of those scripts are cited by name from C# doc comments as the
# provenance of a generated table ("extracted by re/extract_mob_drops.py"), so they are part of the
# product's documentation, not scratch.
#
# What is NOT: everything below. Two kinds of thing, both regenerable, ~28 MB between them —
#   1. extracts from the client PAK and the RTK dump (art, palettes, tables, audio, maps)
#   2. captures and renders produced by a probe run (packet dumps, sprite sheets, row-level swing logs)
#
# The rule to apply when adding a file here: if re-running a script would recreate it, it is a byproduct.
# If a human decided it, it is a finding. Findings are small; that is not a coincidence.
# =================================================================================================
re/**/__pycache__/
re/**/*.pyc
re/**/*.jsonl
re/**/*.png
re/**/*.gif
re/**/*.bat
re/**/*.bak
re/**/*.bak.*
re/**/*.csv.*.bak

# Client/RTK extracts: art, palettes, lookup tables, terrain, audio, and the exe backups that
# re/patch_*.py writes before an on-disk binary patch. NEVER commit a full game exe.
re/**/*.epf
re/**/*.pal
re/**/*.tbl
re/**/*.frm
re/**/*.cmp
re/**/*.exe
re/snd/
re/mus/
re/probe_log*.txt
re/nametag_log.txt
re/sound_log.txt
re/str_eng.res
re/*_dat_list.txt
re/interdat_list.txt

# Row-level live-capture tables. Megabyte-scale dumps of one probe session; the finding they produced is
# in docs/4.x/, and the rows themselves say nothing without the harness that read them.
re/auto/swings.csv
re/auto/attempts.csv
re/auto/incoming.csv
re/auto/kills.csv

# Generated reports. Rebuild: re/build_zone_drop_report.py, re/monster-matcher/monster_matcher.py.
re/zone_drop_report.json
re/zone_drop_report.md
re/monster-matcher/monsters.json
re/monster-matcher/atlas_img/
re/monster-matcher/atlas_ref.json
re/monster-matcher/cdx_monsternpc.json

# re/fx/ is 19 MB of Effect.epf extracts and scraped Atlas GIFs. The three CSVs ARE the findings.
re/fx/*
!re/fx/animation_map.csv
!re/fx/spell_animation_join.csv
!re/fx/triage.csv

# Pre-patch backups of client files taken by re/patches/*.py.
re/patches/backups/
